1. SQL STATEMENT CONVERSION SUMMARY
================================================================================

Total SQL statements processed:          7
Successfully converted by DMS MCP tool:  0
Requiring manual intervention:           7
  Reason: DMS statement_conversion_tool consistently failed with 
          "Metadata model creation/conversion did not complete after 15 attempts"
          (4 separate attempts across different statements and configurations)

DMS Schema Mapping Tool: SUCCESSFUL
  - Successfully retrieved target DDLs for Products, ProductHistory, ProductStats
  - Schema mappings used as authoritative reference for manual conversion
  - Target schema: productmanagement_dbo (all lowercase)

Manual Conversion Approach:
  - All schema object names (tables, columns) converted to lowercase per DMS schema mappings
  - SCOPE_IDENTITY() -> RETURNING clause in writable CTE
  - GETDATE() -> clock_timestamp() (matching DMS default mapping)
  - DECLARE @var / SET @var -> restructured to writable CTEs
  - BEGIN TRANSACTION / COMMIT -> writable CTE pattern (PostgreSQL)
  - Window functions (LAG, RANK, PERCENT_RANK, AVG OVER) -> compatible, names lowercased
  - Added ::NUMERIC cast for integer division in StockPercentageOfAverage calculation

